cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this framework in your own work, please cite it as below."
title: "AI Sociology"
abstract: >-
  An open-source reasoning framework about the human position under AI. It delivers a method of
  judgement rather than a set of conclusions: two axioms (attention is finite; objectives diverge),
  a derived main conclusion (AI's capability will keep improving, but whether it aligns with your
  interests will not improve automatically), the eight-question variable checklist, structural
  judgement tools for occupation, human nature, social stratification, anxiety and physical limits,
  and fourteen installable assets across an expert, an expert team and six skills.
type: software
